{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend","id":971596,"title":"On the Failure to Ascend","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T17:21:23-07:00","id":971596,"title":"On the Failure to Ascend","content":"One of the central elements of MtAs is the idea of personal Ascension. In my mind, when a Mage Awakens, their Avatar offers them two choices, enlightenment or power, and they choose based off of their actions when they Awaken. If they choose enlightenment, they achieve Ascension and they, along with their Avatars, join with...something. If they choose power, they gain Arete.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Mages are people who failed to Ascend and who, for whatever reason, decided that power was more important than enlightenment. With each new seeking, however, their Avatar offers them the same choice, enlightenment or power. The majority of Mages, however, are unwilling to select enlightenment because that would mean giving up their power.<br /> <br /> The insanity of Mages, the arrogance and the hubris, is an unconscious compensatory reflex to allow Mages to function in their lives despite the unconscious disappointment for their failure to Ascend (Marauders being an example of how flexible the definition of functionality can be when you are a Mage). Everything about Mage society, their claims of a subjective reality and their justifications of their conspiracies, are an attempt to mask the central factor of a Mages existence, failure. Because, by choosing power over enlightenment, Mages have chosen failure over the joining that would have comes with Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:12:27-07:00","id":971703,"title":"","content":"Sorry. but this just isn't how Mage works.<br /> <br /> Mages are not, by default insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:46:54-07:00","id":971726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971703#post971703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. but this just isn't how Mage works.<br /> <br /> Mages are not, by default insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis, also failing a seeking isn't the end of the world, sometimes it's more of an opportunity for pc growth then succeeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:02:35-07:00","id":971733,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about failing a seeking? You have to succeed on a seeking to have a chance to choose whether to accept Ascension or to reject Ascension in exchange for power. Failing a seeking just means your understanding of the nature of reality was insufficient for either choice.<br /> <br /> As for Mages not being insane, I really do not see how Mages are anything but insane by any conventional definition. Every Mage I have seen in the books and in play suffer from a number of mental illnesses. I have seen characters that manifest Antisocial Personality Disorder, Borderline Personality Disorder, Capgras Delusion, Compulsive Personality Disorder, Fregolu Delusion, Narcissitic Personality Disorder, Paranoid Schizophrenia, Psychotic Fugue State, Schizotypal Personality Disorder, and, especially, Shared Paranoid Disorder. I have even seen Ekbom's Syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:07:58-07:00","id":971737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971703#post971703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. but this just isn't how Mage works.<br /> <br /> Mages are not, by default insane.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aya really hates the premise of Mage so s/he's constantly trying to &quot;fix&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:09:04-07:00","id":971739,"title":"","content":"Even <i>Ekbom's Syndome?</i> My God!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:16:20-07:00","id":971742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971733#post971733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about failing a seeking? You have to succeed on a seeking to have a chance to choose whether to accept Ascension or to reject Ascension in exchange for power. Failing a seeking just means your understanding of the nature of reality was insufficient for either choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna go out on a limb and say you are really wrong here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:19:45-07:00","id":971744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971737#post971737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aya really hates the premise of Mage so s/he's constantly trying to &quot;fix&quot; it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that explains things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:09:32-07:00","id":971768,"title":"","content":"I do not hate the premise of Mage, I like the basic premise of Mage, I just seem to have a different idea about the premise than most people. I think that Mage is a tragic game about people who have been driven insane by their desire for power and their inability to Ascend. Other people seem to think it is a game of wish fulfillment and fuzzy bunnies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:30:36-07:00","id":971773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971768#post971768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not hate the premise of Mage, I like the basic premise of Mage, I just seem to have a different idea about the premise than most people. I think that Mage is a tragic game about people who have been driven insane by their desire for power and their inability to Ascend. Other people seem to think it is a game of wish fulfillment and fuzzy bunnies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No you've invented that premise wholesale because its not there. Its like Saying vampire is game about people who aren't moral enough to commit Suicide. Yes an argument can be made from the setting details but that's not intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:44:54-07:00","id":971776,"title":"","content":"Not at all. Vampire is a game of immortal predators who have to balance retaining their remaining Humanity against the pleasure of preying on human beings. For the most part, vampires chose to feed on human beings even though most of them are not required to feed on human blood more than once a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:56:51-07:00","id":971781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971776#post971776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. Vampire is a game of immortal predators who have to balance retaining their remaining Humanity against the pleasure of preying on human beings. For the most part, vampires chose to feed on human beings even though most of them are not required to feed on human blood more than once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the inevitability of frenzy, the only moral action a kindred can take is self destruction anything else is delusion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:27:25-07:00","id":971827,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting approach to take for a houserule, if you want to take that particular contrarian reinterpretation of the game.<br /> <br /> Then again, given the relative lack of people just vanishing into an unknown state of transcendence, there might be some other knock-on effects that need handling to implement it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:12:25-07:00","id":971841,"title":"","content":"I can see where the idea comes from, though at least in the baseline game, that seems to be true of the Spheres but not Arete.<br /> <br /> The point with Arete is that it actually is enlightenment. But at any stage, if you want to use that enlightenment for power, that risks trapping you and stop you from increasing your arete again.<br /> <br /> That's the tragedy/horror of it, the archmasters wiped out by the Paradox Storm were comparatively far more enlightenend but that doesn't mean they weren't as trapped as anyone else; maybe more so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:14:30-07:00","id":971852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971733#post971733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mages not being insane, I really do not see how Mages are anything but insane by any conventional definition. Every Mage I have seen in the books and in play suffer from a number of mental illnesses. I have seen characters that manifest Antisocial Personality Disorder, Borderline Personality Disorder, Capgras Delusion, Compulsive Personality Disorder, Fregolu Delusion, Narcissitic Personality Disorder, Paranoid Schizophrenia, Psychotic Fugue State, Schizotypal Personality Disorder, and, especially, Shared Paranoid Disorder. I have even seen Ekbom's Syndrome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful there. Mental illness and insanity are not the same thing. You can have mental difficulties without being insane. I don't think this was an implication you meant to make. <br /> <br /> Also, mental illness is usually something that people are afflicted with. People with said conditions cannot help being anxious, obsessive compulsive, or schizophrenic. Their brain is just wired that way, and for the more gravely afflicted, they have to constantly battle in order to keep some form of functional normalcy.<br /> <br /> Mage, however, is all about choice, and how free reign with choice can ultimately lead to ones downfall if not restrained. A powerful mage can choose to do amazing and terrible things. There are limits, but they can choose to work with or against the constraints of reality to achieve their goals. Because of this power, they are fundamentally different from humans. It's the whole idea of &quot;Justice is for the weak&quot;. Normal behaviour patterns by sleeper standards don't really apply, and what may seem like an act of narcissism to us is pretty much just making breakfast for them, they live in a world with fewer constraints. And if you are unconstrained, what reason is there to hold back? That's the key question in Mage. While Mages are the most human characters in WoD, they have the capacity to be the most monstrous. Perhaps their actions are even more atrocious because they always have the choice not to be. Unlike Vampires driven by fear of Frenzy, or Werewolves driven by uncontrollable Rage, the only thing pushing the mage forward is their own desire for more. <br /> <br /> This is why I find Marauders to be such an interesting and ultimately sympathetic group. They are so consumed by their own internal conflicts and resolutions that they have lost any semblance of choice. They can't turn off their magic, they can't choose to work within the confines of reality. Reality has, in essence, given up on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:20:43-07:00","id":971902,"title":"","content":"To take a real-world example: let's pretend Christian tradition didn't prohibit suicide. Would you expect every Christian to spend a couple of days settling their spiritual and material affairs and then kill themselves? They would believe they were going to Heaven, the most perfect state they can achieve. Why wouldn't they hasten to it?<br /> <br /> I don't think they would. Even if someone believes in it, I don't think people are usually ready to rush headlong into such a fundamental change in their existence. You could call it fear or a reluctance to give up power; in either case, assuming a firm belief in their next life, the desire to delay would be irrational but I think very common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:15:32-07:00","id":971961,"title":"","content":"That was the reason for the suicide prohibition in the proto-Church (it did not come into effect until the early 3rd century AD in the proto-Church, if I remember correctly). People were committing suicide in droves after they helped spread Christianity because they could not wait to get to Heaven. The rate of suicide was so high that the ancient proto-Church had to explicitly forbid it because it is not explicitly forbidden in the ancient Bible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:13:51-07:00","id":971990,"title":"","content":"It misses the point of Ascension completely. If Ascension is merely a choice that the mages <i>did not</i> choose, with that being the <i>beginning</i> of their journey, then why is it the expressed goal of the experience? Should we keep playing a game where the end narrative is &quot;lol, you could of but didn't, sux 2 b u.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Mage is a pretty open-ended game, Ascension is still the path that each mage walks. There are pitfalls along the way, such as madness and corruption, and ultimately the temptation by archemastery if they make it that far, and maybe even then a mage never reaches the clarity required for ascending, but it's still the whole point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:03:48-07:00","id":972020,"title":"","content":"I do seem to be in an obvious minority for thinking that Mage is a tragic game about the dangers of arrogance, hubris, and pride, where Mages will eventually be driven insane by their desire for power as they resist their Avatar's attempts to lead them to Ascension. To me, Ascension does not seem to be dependent on Arete (or Enlightenment), or else experienced Mages would be more likely to Ascend than beginning Mages. In fact, I think that a beginning Mage seems to be more likely to Ascend than an experienced Mage because they have not yet become addicted to magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:32:09-07:00","id":972033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=972020#post972020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do seem to be in an obvious minority for thinking that Mage is a tragic game about the dangers of arrogance, hubris, and pride, where Mages will eventually be driven insane by their desire for power as they resist their Avatar's attempts to lead them to Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on the line of tragedy and degeneration.<br /> <br /> But, that's not the way it's written in the Canon (at least, from what I read)...so, yeah. We're a minority...perhaps the only two xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:38:01-07:00","id":972038,"title":"","content":"I think it's more that it's not terribly coherent. I've heard Satyros in an interview say explicitly that arete is supposed to mirror ascension. The whole 'transcendence of the need for power' is meant to be a part of raising arete.<br /> <br /> Also, personal acension is horribly solipsistic. Just leave the sleepers to the Technocracy and the Nephandi. That radically cuts against the whole point of Revised, which is that there are actual consequences to not caring about sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:49:32-07:00","id":972046,"title":"","content":"How does Arete reflect the transcendence of the need for power? Arete is mechanically a measure of magical power. Anyway, if every potential Mage accepted Ascension instead of seeking power, there would be no Technocracy or Nephandi to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:00:52-07:00","id":972085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=972046#post972046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Arete reflect the transcendence of the need for power? Arete is mechanically a measure of magical power. Anyway, if every potential Mage accepted Ascension instead of seeking power, there would be no Technocracy or Nephandi to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arete is understanding of the universe, the problem is the universe is very complex. There's so much room for tragedy. I mean perhaps the Technocracy is right. The only way humanity can be safe is if we murder all the unicorns. Drive away the fae, close of the gauntlet and kill all the reality Deviants. Is safety worth the price of Freedom? What can you do? What should you do? These are the big questions.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Vampire is a game where God explicitly gives Vampires the &quot;gift&quot; of burning in the sun as an act of mercy so they don't have to commit suicide, there'd be no camarilla to enslave and abuse people. No Sabbat to murder people as a game. If every Vampire would just take God's mercy..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:11:10-07:00","id":972091,"title":"","content":"Arete is explicitly and canonically a measure of <i>enlightenment</i>. Yes, it determines your ability to influence reality, but that's a <i>result</i> of it being a transcendent understanding. That's where your interpretation diverges and becomes noncanonical; you're positing that Arete is instead a form of... Idunno, endarkenment?<br /> <br /> The &quot;tragic game about the dangers of arrogance, hubris, and pride, where Mages will eventually be driven insane by their desire for power&quot; seems from the outside to be you projecting your own expectations and worldview on the gameline. Many mages supposedly follow their Avatar without immediately ascending. And yes, many mages fall into the traps of hubris and arrogance, or are driven power-mad... but that's portrayed as a trap that mages, as humans, have a tendency to fall into. Not as the default state of &quot;being a Mage&quot; as opposed to &quot;being some random person&quot;.<br /> <br /> And you reinterpreting the game that way is fine - as long as you're aware that no, that is not actually what the things are canonically intended to represent, it's a houserule/headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:00:46-07:00","id":972110,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know the fluff of Arete is that it is Enlightenment, but the game mechanics are fairly clear that it is a measure of power. If it was structured like Balance was in MtR, then it would be enlightenment as well as power, but the current game mechanics show how false that position is. Of course, more powerful Mages are going to claim more enlightenment, as they want to justify their status in terms other than 'I rule because I have the biggest stick'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:22:54-07:00","id":972126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=972110#post972110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know the fluff of Arete is that it is Enlightenment, but the game mechanics are fairly clear that it is a measure of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I'm saying your position is a contrarian one. It is a deliberate rejection of core aspects of the way Mage is portrayed and imposing of an alternate interpretation. Much like taking the Technocracy as being the 'real' protagonists and the Traditions as crazy threats to reality itself. It is not the authorially intended portrayal, which is what it very much sounds like you're claiming when you claim that it's what the game is &quot;about&quot;.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the lack of Balance-like mechanics is (a) a bad comparison given that the Balance mechanic didn't exist at the time, (b) very much shoehorning enlightenment into a singular track, which is very much <i>not</i> fitting for a game like Mage where, no, you're <i>not</i> expected to cleave to the One True Morality in your quest for enlightenment. Its acting as a power stat means that the measure of enlightenment is <i>supposed to</i> also be a measure of power, because the former gives shape to the latter.<br /> <br /> If you want to posit that Gnosis isn't canonically connection to the greater spiritual world because it acts as a power stat, you're free to do that as well, but that doesn't mean that you're <i>not</i> giving a contrarian reinterpretation of what the things mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-18-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:36:08-07:00","id":972131,"title":"","content":"There is nothing contradictory about Gnosis being a power stat and access to the spirit world because Fera do not Ascend. If Arete truly represented enlightenment and reflected the ability to Ascend, then an Arete 5 Nephandi would be more likely to Ascend than an Arete 1 Tradition Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:22:56-07:00","id":972158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=972020#post972020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do seem to be in an obvious minority for thinking that Mage is a tragic game about the dangers of arrogance, hubris, and pride, where Mages will eventually be driven insane by their desire for power as they resist their Avatar's attempts to lead them to Ascension. To me, Ascension does not seem to be dependent on Arete (or Enlightenment), or else experienced Mages would be more likely to Ascend than beginning Mages. In fact, I think that a beginning Mage seems to be more likely to Ascend than an experienced Mage because they have not yet become addicted to magical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not. The journey that mages take is fraught with temptation, and often leads to hubristically using their powers and seeking greater power for the sake of that power. That's probably why archemastery precludes ascension, or at least as far as the rules in Masters of the Art are concerned. Of course, opinions are pretty varied about that book and its usefulness and contribution to the game.<br /> <br /> You're also not wrong on your feelings about how Arete is related to likelihood to Ascend. There are anecdotes in some books (I can't remember which) that refer to relatively newly Awakened, fairly weak mages poofing off into some manner of Ascension, whereas masters (not necessarily Archemasters) are stuck looking for the answers. It's all rather personal, and it's quite likely that Ascension isn't the same for everyone, that each's enlightenment is specific to their personal experiences and beliefs. <br /> <br /> Raising Arete, going towards greater &quot;enlightenment,&quot; in this case I think is more a case of coming to greater understandings of the workings of reality and the effects of their Will. However, mages are just as likely to find a sort of circular affirmation as they are to break down their own walls of belief to broader horizons. Given that the true meaning of Ascension and how to achieve it are never clearly defined, you can make it whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:30:58-07:00","id":972253,"title":"","content":"Every World of Darkness series has it's themes.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, you have blood-drinking abominations cursed by god dealing with the cut-throat politics of the immortal as they fight off their own feral nature to try and remain civilized. Hold onto the last dregs of their humanity, or alternatively, give that up for a civilized ideal closer to what their new reality asks of them.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, you have shapeshifting defenders of the natural world, fighting a two front war against the forces of modernity and entropy. The system is breaking down and the enemies are at the gates. What must you do, what sacrifices must you make to save the world?<br /> <br /> Less sure on Wraith, Changeling, and Demon, but I'm sure someone can fill in those.<br /> <br /> In Mage? You have ordinary men or women who gain an understanding of the universe so potent they can alter the fundamental laws of reality. What do they believe? What will they use that power for? And what happens when they disagree? The concept of mage is a fundamentally human concept. It's human history flanderized beyond all belief as men and women go to war time and time again over ideology and resources. Over religion and the lack thereof. Over ethics. Sure, you get cool powers. But so do the people who think your version of cool powers are powered by satan and you need to die. Mage has no morality stat, because to do so you would need to find one morality that all mages subscribe to. Which is quite obviously, impossible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:34:38-07:00","id":972689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971768#post971768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not hate the premise of Mage, I like the basic premise of Mage, I just seem to have a different idea about the premise than most people. I think that Mage is a tragic game about people who have been driven insane by their desire for power and their inability to Ascend. Other people seem to think it is a game of wish fulfillment and fuzzy bunnies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insanity is found in Mages as well as in Sleepers and in more or less the same proportion. I do not understand from where you get that idea. This is not at all what the game describes in the setting. Ascending and growing in power are not contradictory if it does not hurt your own paradigm. The most obvious exemple of that in my opinion is the Might is Right kind of Mage. However, I agree that the ascetic Akashic brother would argue in your way. Hubris might prevent the Ascension, and insanity is the tragic path of some Mages, but there's no way you can generalize that.<br /> <br /> That said, you can obviously give your chronicles the mood you want and your idea is totally interesting. Myself, I often give another kind of tragic mood to the WoD: I like the idea of the escathological world and therefore I often emphasize the inevitability of events. Though, you can not say that Ascension is a struggle between power and enlightment. It may be for some Mages, but defenitely not for all. Enlightment is a path to Ascension and power is just a consequence of the understanding of reality. Both are not opposite. I agree, you can lose yourself in the contemplation of your own powers, but Hubris is a risk and not a fatality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=971768#post971768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, Mages are people who failed to Ascend and who, for whatever reason, decided that power was more important than enlightenment</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, this is the most inaccurate thing you stated. I believe it's the contrary. Mages are the ones who got the possibility to Ascend. In a way, what they do with that gift defines their Path of Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:31:32-07:00","id":972723,"title":"","content":"Do Mages with higher Arete have a greater chance of Ascending than Mages with lower Arete? If they do, then Arete measures 'enlightenment' as well as magical power. If they do not, then Arete only measures magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:37:57-07:00","id":972732,"title":"","content":"I understand you when you say that Arete is a measure of power. After all, it's the only stat we roll to do anything magic, and magic is the single most powerful mechanic in the game. I also understand when people say it's a measure of &quot;enlightenment&quot; because for all intents and purposes that's how it's described in the source material.<br /> <br /> However, I ascribe to the school of thought that states that high Arete is NOT the path to Ascension. Here's my reasoning.<br /> <br /> I agree that Arete is a measure of &quot;enlightenment&quot;, but I'd like to define it a bit more thoroughly than this. Arete is a measure of ones understanding of how they fit in with reality. The more Arete one gets, the greater they understand their place in reality and how their presence can manipulate said reality. It's a measure not of the strength of their will, but their ability to use said will to remake the world they way they wish for it.<br /> <br /> It's also a more esoteric sense on how the universe functions. It starts with the vague awareness that reality is malleable, and eventually grows to having more of a sense that they, as humans, are the ones shaping reality in the first place, until they are able to understand that reality is simply the very essence of human will. The more Arete one has, the greater their ability to understand these concepts. Not just know them, but actually understand and utilise their teachings. There is a big difference.<br /> <br /> You might then conclude that the more one understands the nature of the universe, the easier it is to Ascend. But I would argue against this. It's true that at the highest levels of Arete, the mage gains an insight unparalleled with anything a lower ranked mage could possibly conceive, and their mastery of manipulating this reality with mere will alone is staggering. But here's the crux of the issue. Their understanding is squarely placed within this reality, and as such is limited within its confines. They get so familiar with it all that it becomes harder and harder to decouple from this world and move on to the next. While Ascension may be impossible without a good level of Arete in order to understand it, the higher up the chart you go, the more dependent on your understanding you become.<br /> <br /> This is the tragic fate of the Archmage, so very powerful, but only powerful within the confines of the reality which traps them. They pursue ever greater lengths of power and influence, but do so on the assumption that this understanding of reality is the be all and end all of existence, perhaps under the false impression that &quot;to know&quot; and &quot;to be capable of everything&quot; is what is required in order to ascend.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell. There comes a point where a greater level of &quot;enlightnemnet&quot; or understanding of the nature of reality becomes so all consuming that the mage is unable to imagine anything beyond the reality they've spent their whole life trying to understand.<br /> <br /> A lot of mages would be loath to admit this, because it essentially means that their emphasis on gaining Arete through study, hardship, pilgrimage or what have you, is ultimately futile in the grand scheme of things. It then becomes a form of Effort Justification. The Archmages continue to teach the newer groups that they must become like themselves in order to achieve a chance at Ascension. They may even tell themselves that. After all, who would spend all their life studying and working at something for a goal only to then admit to themselves that it was all a waste of time?<br /> <br /> But that is what I believe is necessary for true ascension. You have to look at all this potential you have, all this power and all this understanding, this &quot;enlightenment&quot; and realise that ultimately it is all confined within this one specific piece of reality, and that to keep ones head in this reality will ultimately tie you to it indefinitely. To ascend then is to let go entirely, to attain understanding, and then be both humble and insightful enough to recognise that it is nothing, and that even this great expanse of knowledge is but a speck, only correct &quot;here&quot;. To ascend is to no longer need or have ties with the &quot;here&quot;.<br /> <br /> With this view, I'd say that yes, Arete is Enlightenment, but to pursue it doggedly will also prevent you from being able to ascend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:57:50-07:00","id":973369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=972723#post972723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Mages with higher Arete have a greater chance of Ascending than Mages with lower Arete? If they do, then Arete measures 'enlightenment' as well as magical power. If they do not, then Arete only measures magical power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its more a biproduct of being closer to Ascension. Each successful Seeking is a step closer to ascension. And each succesful seeking comes with a point of Arete/Enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:58:16-07:00","id":973410,"title":"","content":"Then is a high Arete Nephandi Mage more likely to Ascend than a low Arete Tradition Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:19:02-07:00","id":973428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=973410#post973410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then is a high Arete Nephandi Mage more likely to Ascend than a low Arete Tradition Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>*facepalm*<br /> <br /> Apply the same argument but substituting the phrase &quot;Ascension or Descension&quot; for &quot;Ascension&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it also applies to Technocrats despite them using the game term &quot;Enlightenment&quot; instead of &quot;Arete&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:30:51-07:00","id":973437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=973410#post973410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then is a high Arete Nephandi Mage more likely to Ascend than a low Arete Tradition Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No because they have an inverted avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:45:53-07:00","id":973450,"title":"","content":"not much of a mage person but... I'd always understood mages to need an Arete of 10 to ascend, is that not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:48:44-07:00","id":973453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=973450#post973450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not much of a mage person but... I'd always understood mages to need an Arete of 10 to ascend, is that not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. A Mage with lower Arete can potentially Ascend (there's fiction to that effect), whatever it is you think Ascension means. There aren't strict game-mechanical requirements on it, and what is actually entailed is left very much to individual interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:18:17-07:00","id":973469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971596-on-the-failure-to-ascend?p=973410#post973410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then is a high Arete Nephandi Mage more likely to Ascend than a low Arete Tradition Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>This very question suggests a fundamental misunderstanding on what Nephandi are and how they function.<br /> <br /> So, you've probably already guessed my answer to this is &quot;No&quot;. Partially because of what I wrote above about how Arete does not lead to Ascension.<br /> <br /> But the main reason is because Nephandi just plain and simple cannot ascend, and can never ascend. They gave it up the moment they went through the cauls and no amount of Arete is going to change that. Their inverted avatars prevent them from ever being able to ascend, their path is now fixed towards oblivion or bust. Either the world dies, or they die, and even then they'll just come back to break the world some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}